# Lintian overrides for voice-to-text source package
#
# voice-to-text ships a pre-built Rust binary (vtt.prebuilt) because
# Ubuntu Noble LTS cargo 1.75 can't parse the edition-2024 manifests that
# modern Rust crates use — building from source on Launchpad's Noble
# builders is structurally impossible without bundling a newer toolchain.
# See debian/rules header for the full rationale.
#
# Google Chrome, Zoom, Slack, and most proprietary .debs follow this
# same "ship the prebuilt binary, let shlibdeps generate Depends" pattern.
# The lintian "source-is-missing" complaint is expected and documented.
#
# The binary IS auditable — the full Rust source is in src/ alongside
# the prebuilt, built with scripts/build-release.sh from the committed
# Cargo.lock. The release scripts build the prebuilt at release time from
# the tagged source and pack it into the source package; it is never
# committed to git.

